# Maps directories to reviewers, matching the server/discord_client/webapp/ops
# module split (see PUBLISHING_PLAN.md). GitHub auto-requests these owners as
# reviewers on any PR touching a matching path; the LAST matching pattern
# wins, so more specific paths belong below more general ones.
#
# Replace the placeholder @usernames below with real GitHub usernames before
# this has any effect -- CODEOWNERS entries that don't resolve to a real user
# (or a team the repo owner belongs to) are silently ignored, not an error.

# Default: repo owner reviews anything not claimed by a more specific rule below.
*                       @Delta-43

# Backend product (agent, API, rules/scryfall MCP servers).
/server/                @Delta-43 @dev-tester-1 @dev-tester-2

# Discord bot client.
/discord_client/        @Delta-43 @dev-tester-1 @dev-tester-2

# PWA frontend.
/webapp/                @Delta-43 @dev-tester-1 @dev-tester-2

# Backup/restore + future monitoring config -- the reliability/monitoring owner.
/ops/                   @Delta-43 @ktrileo

# Deployment/orchestration files -- monitoring/reliability should see these too,
# since uptime/alerting config and compose changes are tightly coupled.
/docker-compose.yml     @Delta-43 @ktrileo
/docker-compose.override.yml  @Delta-43 @reliability-owner
/Caddyfile              @Delta-43 @ktrileo

# CI workflows (see PUBLISHING_PLAN.md Stage 0 for the rollout history).
/.github/               @Delta-43 @ktrileo
